PLACEHOLDER — Stripe Apple Pay domain verification
====================================================

To activate Apple Pay (Express Checkout) on web:

1. Stripe Dashboard → Settings → Payment methods → Apple Pay → "Configure"
   → "Add new domain" → enter `ithasfire.com`.
2. Stripe will give you a verification file to download. Open it — it's
   a base64-looking blob of text (one long string, no JSON, no header).
3. REPLACE the entire contents of this file with the contents Stripe gave
   you. Do not add any wrapper text.
4. Deploy.
5. Back in the Stripe dashboard, click "Verify" — Stripe fetches this
   URL and checks the token matches.
6. Repeat for every domain that embeds Stripe Elements (e.g.
   `web-dev.ithasfire.com` for dev, plus any embed host if used).

Notes:
- Served via the next.config.ts headers rule with Content-Type: text/plain.
- Apple Pay button stays hidden in Express Checkout until verification passes.
- Token rotates every ~12 months — Stripe will email you when re-verification
  is needed; replace this file's contents and redeploy.
